      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could this paragraph say what fails without the patch? As far as I can see, in a 4KB process `dma_buf_mmap_internal()` rejects mappings of more than a quarter of the buffer with `-EINVAL`, since `vma_pages()` counts 4KB pages. `system_heap_mmap()` remaps a whole kernel page at each address, so a mapping at a 4KB offset also maps slices of the physically next page, which may not belong to the buffer, and one that ends partway through a page gets PTEs past `vm_end`.\n\nI think \"Preserve the VMA\u0027s file slice when setting vm_pgoff\" can go as well: the patch no longer touches the `vm_pgoff` update in `dma_buf_mmap()`.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "bbe3876eb0a05c0c9cc8b19f9d6c54ec7c977ad8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
