      "side": 1,
      "message": "The clamped loop looks right to me, thanks. One follow-up to the loop I suggested on PS7, now that we keep slice math in P3S headers: would you mind moving it into a small helper in `include/linux/p3s/vma.h`? Something like:\n\n```\n/* Bytes from @addr to the end of the kernel page that backs it, within @vma */\nstatic inline unsigned long vma_kernel_page_bytes(const struct vm_area_struct *vma,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t  unsigned long addr)\n{\n\treturn min(PAGE_SIZE_KERNEL - vma_folio_offset(vma, addr),\n\t\t   vma-\u003evm_end - addr);\n}\n```\n\nThen `system_heap_mmap()` only needs a `size` local, with no `off`, and the rest of the loop stays as it is now:\n\n```\n\t\tunsigned long size \u003d vma_kernel_page_bytes(vma, addr);\n```\n\nNative VMAs get `min(PAGE_SIZE, vm_end - addr)`, so it needs no stub.",
